  "seams": [
    "Existing engine local-state home resolver and OS file reads/writes are injected; source reuses benilla_app::config_dir and the existing atomic writer. No new generic engine implementation.",
    "Scratch allocation/free, CRT memory operations, string-vector growth, final assignment formatting and LF join are injected library seams. Original line iteration/replacement/Unicode trim/read dispatch execute from the installed PE.",
    "The VM lookup executes through assignment formatting and stops before the Lua/compiler bridge. Caller cases enter immediately after the completed file write and stop at VM assignment, inactive cleanup or the missing-client panic route.",
    "Current raw Ghidra imports omit external jump tables and use generic ABI; assembly and the retained current read table establish actual dispatch.",
    "Source route guards are inspection checks. Rust tests, compilation, actual OS persistence, UI/Lua lifecycle and original/rebuilt comparisons were not run."
  ],
